From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:55:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: vdec: a buffer sent as an empty LAST is not
 recycled again

A drain takes a queued CAPTURE buffer for its empty LAST without the
microcode knowing: the microcode still counts it free. When the client
queues it again, the recycle tells the microcode a second time, and the
microcode decodes two pictures into it in a row. The second completion
finds the buffer gone: "Buffer 0 done but it doesn't exist in m2m_ctx",
and the client's picture is overwritten.

Mark a buffer sent as an empty LAST and skip its next recycle. A buffer
that only now carries a pending LAST was not recycled yet: recycle it
first. MJPEG and MPEG-4 drained and restarted 15 times gave 23 double
completions, now 1.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/vdec/vdec.c
+++ b/vdec/vdec.c
@@ -718,6 +718,8 @@
 	if (vb->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE && !held &&
 	    READ_ONCE(sess->last_pending)) {
 		WRITE_ONCE(sess->last_pending, false);
+		if (vdec_codec_needs_recycle(sess))
+			vdec_queue_recycle(sess, vb);
 		amvdec_dst_buf_done_empty_last(sess);
 		return;
 	}
@@ -734,7 +736,9 @@
 
 	if (sess->streamon_cap &&
 	    vb->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE &&
-	    vdec_codec_needs_recycle(sess))
+	    vdec_codec_needs_recycle(sess) &&
+	    !(vb->index < VIDEO_MAX_FRAME &&
+	      test_and_clear_bit(vb->index, sess->last_unused)))
 		vdec_queue_recycle(sess, vb);
 
 }
@@ -901,6 +905,7 @@
 		list_del(&tmp->list);
 		kfree(tmp);
 	}
+	bitmap_zero(sess->last_unused, VIDEO_MAX_FRAME);
 }
 
 static void vdec_stop_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q)
--- a/vdec/vdec.h
+++ b/vdec/vdec.h
@@ -430,6 +430,8 @@
 	u32 last_offset;
 	u32 wrap_count;
 	u32 fw_idx_to_vb2_idx[32];
+	/* CAPTURE buffers sent as an empty LAST: still free in the microcode */
+	DECLARE_BITMAP(last_unused, VIDEO_MAX_FRAME);
 
 	enum amvdec_status status;
 	void *priv;
--- a/vdec/vdec_helpers.c
+++ b/vdec/vdec_helpers.c
@@ -572,6 +572,8 @@
 	if (!vbuf)
 		return false;
 
+	if (vbuf->vb2_buf.index < VIDEO_MAX_FRAME)
+		set_bit(vbuf->vb2_buf.index, sess->last_unused);
 	for (plane = 0; plane < vbuf->vb2_buf.num_planes; plane++)
 		vb2_set_plane_payload(&vbuf->vb2_buf, plane, 0);
 	vbuf->vb2_buf.timestamp = 0;
